soc: sunxi: cpu_comm: the reload path on real hardware

Originally: "soc: sunxi: cpu_comm/h713-mips: the reload path on real hardware - only requested hardware locks, word stores into the shared region, the firmware where the image keeps it (02.10.2026, device test B3)"

Two faults on the first device runs of the reload: cpu_comm_firmware_reset() released all 14 hardware
spinlocks although only some are requested (NULL -> Oops in __hwspin_unlock), and comm_InitSpinLock()
- the master init path, never run on the ARM before - wrote the 12 spinlock entries with plain pointer
stores that the compiler merges into 16-byte stores, an alignment fault on the ioremap()ed shared region
(work/FB-MIPSRELOAD/device/oops-*.log, oops2-*.log). Now: only requested locks, writel per word, and the
default firmware path /boot/mips/display.bin where our image carries it. Applies after 0167/0167a and STANDBY 0172.

Rebased onto the R1 series (0224), applies cleanly. The third part, the
default path /boot/mips/display.bin in sun50i-h713-mips.c, is not here: that
driver is new in this series (0231) and carries the path from the start.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm.h
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm.h
@@ -628,6 +628,7 @@ void comm_SpinLocksetType(int lock_id, int type);
 int  spinlockhwReg(int lock_id);
 int  tryspinlockhwReg(int lock_id);
 void spinUnlockhwReg(int lock_id);
+bool cpu_comm_hwlock_requested(int lock_id);
 int  getShareRegbyID(int reg_id);
 int  getInterruptRegChannel(u32 cpu, u32 channel);
 void ResetCommInterrupt(int dummy);
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_dev.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_dev.c
@@ -1321,7 +1321,8 @@ int cpu_comm_firmware_reset(void)
 	blocking_notifier_call_chain(&cpu_comm_fw_chain,
 				     CPU_COMM_FIRMWARE_HALTED, NULL);
 	for (i = 0; i < 14; i++)	/* whatever the dead core held is stale */
-		spinUnlockhwReg(i);
+		if (cpu_comm_hwlock_requested(i))	/* only the locks this side holds a handle for */
+			spinUnlockhwReg(i);
 	/* The vendor's InitCommMem zeroes magic1 .. magic2 before it rebuilds. */
 	memset_io((void __iomem *)(ShMemAddrBase + SHMEM_OFF_MAGIC1), 0,
 		  SHMEM_OFF_MAGIC2 + 4 - SHMEM_OFF_MAGIC1);
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_hw.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_hw.c
@@ -763,6 +763,12 @@ void spinUnlockhwReg(int lock_id)
 	__hwspin_unlock(hwlocks[lock_id], HWLOCK_RAW, NULL);
 }
 
+/* Does this side hold a handle for hardware lock @lock_id? (deep review 02.10.2026: not all 14 are requested) */
+bool cpu_comm_hwlock_requested(int lock_id)
+{
+	return lock_id >= 0 && lock_id < HW_SPINLOCK_COUNT && hwlocks[lock_id] != NULL;
+}
+
 /* ── Software Spinlocks (in shared memory) ─────────────────── */
 
 /*
@@ -844,14 +850,20 @@ int comm_InitSpinLock(int dummy)
 	 * makes the init atomic; dmb(ish) ensures visibility to MIPS before we
 	 * release HW lock 0 (which signals MIPS to proceed). */
 	for (i = 0; i < 12; i++) {
-		u32 *entry = (u32 *)(base + SPINLOCK_ENTRY_SIZE * i);
-
-		entry[0] = SPINLOCK_FREE;	/* type */
-		entry[1] = SPINLOCK_FREE;	/* status */
-		entry[2] = 0;			/* mutex_flag */
-		entry[3] = SPINLOCK_FREE;	/* owner_cpu = free */
-		writel(0, entry + 4);	/* ref_count */
-		writel(SPINLOCK_HWID_NONE, entry + 8); /* thread_id */
+		void __iomem *entry = (void __iomem *)(base + SPINLOCK_ENTRY_SIZE * i);
+
+		/*
+		 * One 32-bit store per word: the region is ioremap()ed Device
+		 * memory, and plain pointer stores get merged by the compiler into
+		 * 16-byte stores, which fault there (alignment fault at +12 on the
+		 * reload path, 02.10.2026, work/FB-MIPSRELOAD/device/oops2-*.log).
+		 */
+		writel_relaxed(SPINLOCK_FREE, entry + 0);	/* type */
+		writel_relaxed(SPINLOCK_FREE, entry + 4);	/* status */
+		writel_relaxed(0, entry + 8);			/* mutex_flag */
+		writel_relaxed(SPINLOCK_FREE, entry + 12);	/* owner_cpu = free */
+		writel(0, entry + 16);				/* ref_count (as before: entry + 4 words) */
+		writel(SPINLOCK_HWID_NONE, entry + 32);		/* thread_id (as before: entry + 8 words) */
 	}
 	dmb(ish);
 
